<h2 id="modules-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="01AD">17.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
In this chapter we work out basic notions of sheaves of modules. This in particular includes the case of abelian sheaves, since these may be viewed as sheaves of $\underline{\mathbf{Z}}$-modules. Basic references are <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/FAC">FAC</a>]</span>, <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/EGA">EGA</a>]</span> and <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/SGA4">SGA4</a>]</span>. 
</p>
<p>
We work out what happens for sheaves of modules on ringed topoi in another chapter (see Modules on Sites, Section <a href="/tag/03A5" data-tag="03A5">18.1</a>), although there we will mostly just duplicate the discussion from this chapter. 
</p>
